    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a disposable-email-domain blocklist that rejects owner creation/update with a **400** when the email's domain is `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, or `guerrillamail.com`.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (not Spring MVC controllers), I added:\n\n1. **`ValidateOwnerEmailDomain`** (function step) \u2014 reads the validated `OwnerFieldsDto` via `@Val`, extracts the domain after the last `@`, and throws a checked `DisposableEmailDomainException` if it's blocklisted. Email is optional so null/blank is skipped; syntactic validity is already enforced upstream by the `@Email` constraint at `ValidateOwner`. It runs *after* `NormalizeOwnerEmail`, so the address is already lower-cased (and it also lower-cases defensively).\n\n2. **`DisposableEmailDomainException`** \u2014 a checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n\n3. **`DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler`** + escalation YAML (`officefloor/escalation/...DisposableEmailDomainException.yml`) \u2014 responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail`, matching the existing `InvalidPostcodeException` pattern.\n\n4. **Wiring** \u2014 inserted the `validateEmailDomain` step right after `normalizeEmail` in both `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` (carrying `govern: [ transaction ]` on the PUT step to match its neighbors).\n\nTest results: the new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` passes, and the full suite is **BUILD SUCCESS** (1 test, 0 failures).",
