    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a faithful, additive mirror of the patterns already established in this codebase:\n\n- **`ValidateOwnerEmailDomain`** is structurally identical to its sibling `ValidateOwnerPostcode`: a single `service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto)` method, the same \"optional when absent \u2192 early return\" guard idiom, the same class-level Javadoc explaining what upstream constraint already covers the invalid case, and a `static final` blocklist as the local source of truth. Logic sits in the right unit \u2014 one validation concern per function class.\n- **`DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler`** matches `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` line-for-line in shape and correctly reuses the shared `ProblemDetails.build(...)` helper rather than re-inventing the ProblemDetail assembly \u2014 no duplication.\n- **`DisposableEmailDomainException`** mirrors the other checked escalation exceptions (single `String` ctor, extends `Exception`, doc pointing at its thrower and handler).\n- The escalation YAML and the two pipeline edits follow the documented `<path>.<METHOD>.yml` / `escalation/<FQCN>.yml` conventions. Placement after `normalizeEmail` (so the domain compare is case-insensitive) is deliberate and documented, and the PUT variant correctly carries `govern: [ transaction ]` to stay consistent with its surrounding steps.\n\nNo catch-all is forming, nothing is duplicated, and the naming (`Validate\u2026`, handler/exception pairing) is exactly what a maintainer here would expect. Structure is clean.",
